Chapter: EffectWidenScopeCross

Section: Body

 One channel handed over for a DIFFERENT channel. Neither contains the
 other, and this refusal is the channel family's ANSWER rather than the
 absence of one: scope-subsumes asks a Console scope whether it contains
 another, and a channel contains only itself.

 That is what makes this different from its filesystem sibling, which is
 the same shape and is ACCEPTED: effect-widen-scope-narrow hands
 "/config/app/" to a "/config/" parameter and passes, because a path does
 contain what extends it. One relation, asked of two families, two
 answers. Run both through a single text-starts-with and "stdout" would
 sit inside "std".

  stdout-print : Text -> [Console "stdout"] Nothing
  stdout-print (t) = act
    print-line-uni t
  end

  apply-auth : (Text -> [Console "auth"] Nothing), Text -> [Console "auth"] Nothing
  apply-auth (f) (t) = act
    f t
  end

  opening : [Console "auth"] Nothing = act
    apply-auth stdout-print "crossed"
  end
